--- GATE SCRIPT DEFECT ANALYSIS (Honesty Covenant: no red-as-green, no silent drift) ---
The gate computes:  $missing = @($required | Where-Object { $all -notmatch $_ })
PowerShell's array -notmatch operator returns the SUBSET of elements that do NOT match,
not a boolean. Whenever $all contains >1 differing line, ($all -notmatch <marker>) is a
non-empty array, which is truthy, so EVERY marker is misclassified as "missing".
Proof of operator semantics:
  Example: 'Generated' IS present in source, yet  ($all -notmatch 'Generated').Count = 1  (non-empty => truthy => mis-flagged "missing")
  This defect reports MISSING=8 even on an untouched tree (reproduced independently).
Corrected predicate:  Where-Object { -not ($all -match $_) }  => MISSING_DATA_MARKERS_CORRECTED=0.
Per-marker match counts above show all 8 required markers are genuinely present (every count > 0).

